<title>SYRIA: Syria produces 725,000 tonnes of raw cotton.</title>
<headline>Syria produces 725,000 tonnes of raw cotton.</headline>
<dateline>DAMASCUS 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syria's raw cotton output rose to a record of 725,000 tonnes this year, up from around 650,000 in 1995, Ahmed Suhad Jubara, chief of the state-owned cotton marketing organisation (CMO), said on Monday.</p>
<p>He told Reuters the CMO, the sole marketer of cotton in Syria, was planning to export 125,000 tonnes of ginned cotton from this year's outturn.</p>
</text>
